00:00:05,385 --> 00:02:05,385
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:10,285 --> 00:02:11,805
Episode 94

3
00:02:11,945 --> 00:02:13,525
Allah!

4
00:02:13,605 --> 00:02:18,765
Allah! Allah! Allah! Allah!

5
00:02:25,085 --> 00:02:29,825
Allah! Allah! Allah! Allah!

6
00:02:29,925 --> 00:02:32,725
Allah! Allah! Allah! Allah!

7
00:03:10,305 --> 00:03:13,845
Inegöl will be your grave, Osman Bey!

8
00:03:14,265 --> 00:03:15,525
Your grave!

9
00:03:47,805 --> 00:03:51,085
Soldiers! Defend the castle!

10
00:03:51,085 --> 00:03:52,825
With your lives!

11
00:03:53,045 --> 00:03:59,565
Allah is one! Allah is one! Allah is one!

12
00:06:35,685 --> 00:06:42,025
Allah is one! Allah is one! Allah is one!

13
00:07:15,775 --> 00:07:20,315
Allah is one! Allah is one! Allah is one!

14
00:07:25,315 --> 00:07:27,645
Allah is one! Allah is one! Allah is one!

15
00:07:39,115 --> 00:07:42,685
Allah is one! Allah is one! Allah is one!

16
00:07:53,105 --> 00:07:55,185
For Rome!

17
00:08:47,825 --> 00:08:51,025
Today is the day for matyrdom!

18
00:08:51,385 --> 00:08:53,905
Allah is one! Allah is one! Allah is one!

19
00:09:05,025 --> 00:09:08,555
Show mercy to those who seek!
Draw your swords to those who seek wrath!

20
00:09:08,625 --> 00:09:10,185
Come on, alps!

21
00:09:10,265 --> 00:09:17,575
Allah is one! Allah is one! Allah is one!

22
00:09:50,065 --> 00:09:52,065
Come on, lions!

23
00:09:52,105 --> 00:09:53,645
Come on!

24
00:09:55,345 --> 00:09:57,925
Allah is one!

25
00:10:19,605 --> 00:10:21,105
Allah is one!

26
00:10:53,445 --> 00:10:54,985
Gündüz Bey!

27
00:10:55,985 --> 00:10:58,465
Today is the day.

28
00:10:59,345 --> 00:11:02,165
Allah is one!

29
00:11:13,425 --> 00:11:15,245
Gündüz Bey!

30
00:11:27,265 --> 00:11:29,045
Gündüz Bey!

31
00:11:34,305 --> 00:11:36,345
Gündüz Bey!

32
00:11:38,205 --> 00:11:39,885
Gündüz Bey!

33
00:11:41,545 --> 00:11:43,045
Gündüz Bey!

34
00:11:44,585 --> 00:11:45,965
Gündüz Bey!

35
00:11:46,025 --> 00:11:47,545
Gündüz Bey!

36
00:11:47,565 --> 00:11:48,865
Gündüz Bey!

37
00:11:48,865 --> 00:11:49,685
My Bey!

38
00:11:49,705 --> 00:11:52,285
Are you all right, my Bey?

39
00:11:52,345 --> 00:11:53,195
We will take...

40
00:11:53,195 --> 00:11:55,195
...the castle! I won't leave you!

41
00:11:55,245 --> 00:11:57,365
Cerkutay is here!

42
00:11:57,365 --> 00:12:00,065
You are fine, my Bey!
You are fine.

43
00:12:08,865 --> 00:12:10,365
Gündüz Bey!

44
00:12:10,445 --> 00:12:12,965
Gündüz Bey! Gündüz Bey!

45
00:12:13,285 --> 00:12:14,805
Alps!

46
00:12:14,885 --> 00:12:16,905
Fight until there is no infidel left!

47
00:12:16,955 --> 00:12:20,505
Burn the walls, destroy them! Attack!

48
00:12:21,745 --> 00:12:23,325
My Bey!

49
00:12:23,345 --> 00:12:24,705
You are fine!

50
00:12:24,705 --> 00:12:27,785
You are fine, my Bey!

51
00:12:27,875 --> 00:12:31,915
Don't die, please!
You are fine, my Bey!

52
00:13:19,405 --> 00:13:20,925
Nikola!

53
00:14:21,565 --> 00:14:24,085
Soldier!

54
00:14:24,425 --> 00:14:25,925
Retreat!

55
00:14:48,865 --> 00:14:50,365
My Bey!

56
00:14:51,565 --> 00:14:53,645
I know a way to enter from the back!

57
00:14:53,725 --> 00:14:55,245
Come on, then!

58
00:14:59,565 --> 00:15:02,565
Holy Jesus, you made a sacrifice for us.

59
00:15:02,925 --> 00:15:06,425
You paid for the sin of the first man by
crucifixion.

60
00:15:06,865 --> 00:15:09,925
Now, this city is paying the price
because of Nikola.

61
00:15:10,725 --> 00:15:13,285
Father, Son and Holy Spirit.

62
00:15:13,465 --> 00:15:14,965
Protect my people.

63
00:15:15,105 --> 00:15:17,845
Don't make the innocents pay for Lord
Nikola's idiocy.

64
00:15:17,985 --> 00:15:19,525
Amen.

65
00:15:22,765 --> 00:15:25,105
Save yourselves! The Turks are in
Inegöl!

66
00:15:25,105 --> 00:15:26,665
They are everywhere!

67
00:15:26,705 --> 00:15:28,265
Run! Run!

68
00:15:31,205 --> 00:15:33,365
God, remind the Turks of their mercy.

69
00:15:36,550 --> 00:15:37,783
My Bey...

70
00:15:37,785 --> 00:15:39,808
...Nikola filled the door with soldiers.

71
00:15:39,875 --> 00:15:42,415
Nikola's moves are now redundant.

72
00:15:43,050 --> 00:15:45,060
He can't do anything.

73
00:15:46,340 --> 00:15:49,380
We've done a lot of impossible things.

74
00:15:50,170 --> 00:15:52,750
Come on, valiants. Come on!

75
00:17:28,150 --> 00:17:30,200
Noone will pass this door!

76
00:17:30,330 --> 00:17:31,850
No one!

77
00:18:22,295 --> 00:18:25,995
Brother, it was our destiny to fight back
to back and...

78
00:18:26,495 --> 00:18:28,315
...be a martyr.

79
00:18:28,485 --> 00:18:31,605
Thankfully, we die for the conquest,
for Allah.

80
00:18:33,885 --> 00:18:36,775
Sisters! Shoot!

81
00:18:38,405 --> 00:18:40,435
Allah is one!

82
00:18:40,505 --> 00:18:42,435
Attack!

83
00:19:21,965 --> 00:19:23,585
Come on!

84
00:19:55,135 --> 00:19:56,645
Help me!

85
00:19:58,035 --> 00:20:00,025
Let's open this.

86
00:20:12,675 --> 00:20:14,195
He ran away.

87
00:20:15,985 --> 00:20:18,505
Is there a passage here?

88
00:20:33,085 --> 00:20:35,645
Where can he go in his own castle, Turgut
Bey?

89
00:20:36,085 --> 00:20:39,135
That dog must have thought of something.

90
00:20:43,185 --> 00:20:44,695
Nikola.

91
00:20:46,885 --> 00:20:48,425
Nikola.

92
00:21:00,585 --> 00:21:03,145
You can't go anywhere.

93
00:21:04,650 --> 00:21:06,875
Anywhere.

94
00:21:10,885 --> 00:21:12,445
Nephew.

95
00:21:13,050 --> 00:21:15,635
You've been with them for a long time.

96
00:21:16,325 --> 00:21:18,675
You know all about them.

97
00:21:18,785 --> 00:21:21,035
But there is something you don't.

98
00:21:22,540 --> 00:21:25,135
And they hide it very well.

99
00:21:27,485 --> 00:21:29,735
You were like their soldier.

100
00:21:30,140 --> 00:21:32,505
They seem quick.

101
00:21:32,615 --> 00:21:34,495
They seem fearless.

102
00:21:35,485 --> 00:21:37,775
But they are cowards.

103
00:21:41,985 --> 00:21:44,035
And they hide it very well.

104
00:21:48,525 --> 00:21:53,375
They have passages everywhere in case
something happens.

105
00:21:54,250 --> 00:21:56,825
Let's find Nikola before he escapes.

106
00:22:11,405 --> 00:22:13,415
Nikola.

107
00:22:58,950 --> 00:23:01,035
Nikola.

108
00:23:02,375 --> 00:23:07,195
They are such cowards that they even build
they passages...

109
00:23:08,185 --> 00:23:11,075
...under where they sit.

110
00:23:17,585 --> 00:23:19,095
My Bey!

111
00:23:19,625 --> 00:23:21,455
Inegöl has fallen, my Bey.

112
00:23:21,550 --> 00:23:25,405
Our soldiers are flowing through
the walls and gates!

113
00:23:26,685 --> 00:23:28,765
Thanks to Allah!

114
00:23:36,385 --> 00:23:39,885
Nikola's head is all that is left.

115
00:23:40,335 --> 00:23:42,135
Don't worry.

116
00:23:43,085 --> 00:23:44,875
We will take that too.

117
00:23:47,715 --> 00:23:48,935
Turgut Bey.

118
00:23:49,405 --> 00:23:51,575
You stay here and provide security.

119
00:23:51,875 --> 00:23:53,255
Don't, Osman Bey.

120
00:23:53,445 --> 00:23:56,815
Are you going after Nikola alone?

121
00:23:56,895 --> 00:23:58,255
No.

122
00:23:58,995 --> 00:24:01,635
The brave men who gave good news will
come after me.

123
00:24:03,685 --> 00:24:06,865
Aktemur, meet Inegöl's people.
Tell them that...

124
00:24:07,065 --> 00:24:10,745
...no innocent people will be harmed.

125
00:24:11,185 --> 00:24:12,765
As you order, my Bey!

126
00:24:12,835 --> 00:24:14,195
Come on, alps!

127
00:24:14,225 --> 00:24:17,405
Osman Bey, the revenge of the innocent
people depend on you now.

128
00:24:17,585 --> 00:24:20,465
Cut his breath so that they can find
peace.

129
00:24:21,435 --> 00:24:23,385
Nikola has nowhere to run now.

130
00:24:24,885 --> 00:24:26,655
This will be over today.

131
00:24:26,905 --> 00:24:28,415
Thank you.

132
00:24:28,965 --> 00:24:31,125
Come on! In the name of Allah!

133
00:24:46,745 --> 00:24:48,245
Brothers.

134
00:24:49,785 --> 00:24:52,745
The love of Jesus Christ is with us.
Don't worry.

135
00:24:53,305 --> 00:24:56,975
Besides, you know that the Turks took
Bilecik.

136
00:24:57,385 --> 00:25:01,305
But they did not harm any of our
coreligionists there.

137
00:25:02,475 --> 00:25:07,075
The Turks were also friendly to the
Christians living with them in Söğüt.

138
00:25:08,085 --> 00:25:11,585
As long as we don't draw a sword to them,
they will show us mercy.

139
00:25:12,105 --> 00:25:14,385
Don't be afraid, pray.

140
00:25:23,965 --> 00:25:26,495
Trust the Priest.

141
00:25:26,975 --> 00:25:28,555
Don't fear.

142
00:25:29,875 --> 00:25:34,655
Us, Turks, we never hurt the innocents.

143
00:25:35,535 --> 00:25:36,745
On the contrary...

144
00:25:37,925 --> 00:25:41,445
...we stand against those who try to
harm them.

145
00:25:42,835 --> 00:25:46,865
You are the commander who saved me from
the torture in the dungeon.

146
00:25:48,085 --> 00:25:49,975
So, you are a Turk.

147
00:25:50,575 --> 00:25:52,585
I should've known this from your mercy.

148
00:25:55,085 --> 00:25:56,445
Yes.

149
00:25:57,755 --> 00:25:59,805
I'm not a Roman commander.

150
00:26:01,165 --> 00:26:02,675
I am Turkish.

151
00:26:03,445 --> 00:26:05,565
He is a Turk!

152
00:26:06,945 --> 00:26:08,845
But don't worry.

153
00:26:10,175 --> 00:26:15,295
As long as Osman Bey swings the flag of
Islam on these walls...

154
00:26:15,735 --> 00:26:20,045
...you will neither starve nor be hurt.

155
00:26:21,055 --> 00:26:23,205
You will live in good conditions.

156
00:26:23,635 --> 00:26:25,525
Thank you!

157
00:26:26,625 --> 00:26:31,645
Turks do not defeat their enemies with
their swords but with mercy.

158
00:26:32,345 --> 00:26:35,225
Their mercy that is more cruel than their
sword.

159
00:26:37,335 --> 00:26:38,865
Aktemur!

160
00:26:39,825 --> 00:26:41,275
Gündüz Bey...

161
00:26:41,885 --> 00:26:43,845
...is wounded.

162
00:26:52,745 --> 00:26:55,215
Gündüz Bey is wounded, Ayşe Hatun.

163
00:26:55,965 --> 00:26:57,475
Gündüz!

164
00:26:58,865 --> 00:27:00,455
Gündüz!

165
00:27:06,305 --> 00:27:08,875
Drink this, Gündüz Bey.

166
00:27:08,895 --> 00:27:10,655
Open your mouth.

167
00:27:22,715 --> 00:27:24,975
You will recover, my Bey.

168
00:27:25,835 --> 00:27:27,715
You will recover.

169
00:27:29,165 --> 00:27:32,755
We have many infidels to attack like
wolves!

170
00:27:44,325 --> 00:27:45,825
Gündüz!

171
00:27:48,985 --> 00:27:50,565
Gündüz Bey!

172
00:27:53,435 --> 00:27:56,475
Ayşe! Ayşe! Ayşe!

173
00:28:03,015 --> 00:28:04,515
Gündüz!

174
00:28:14,455 --> 00:28:15,765
Father!

175
00:28:24,535 --> 00:28:26,835
Why didn't you take him to the healing
tent?

176
00:28:28,845 --> 00:28:30,815
I am telling you, Cerkutay!

177
00:28:31,195 --> 00:28:33,225
Why is he still here?

178
00:28:34,915 --> 00:28:39,995
Kumral Abdal told us not to move those
who fall and inform me.

179
00:28:41,355 --> 00:28:46,525
We called him, Ayşe Sister. He must be
on his way.

180
00:28:49,495 --> 00:28:53,095
Fall? What fall?

181
00:28:55,915 --> 00:28:57,955
He fell from the wall...

182
00:28:59,835 --> 00:29:01,385
...while fighting.

183
00:29:07,765 --> 00:29:10,275
Gündüz! Gündüz! I am here.

184
00:29:10,345 --> 00:29:11,915
Gündüz, I am here.

185
00:29:12,005 --> 00:29:13,515
Gündüz, I am here.

186
00:29:13,565 --> 00:29:15,135
Gündüz, I am here.

187
00:29:15,225 --> 00:29:18,755
Look, Aktemur is here too. Our son is
here.

188
00:29:21,595 --> 00:29:23,105
Look.

189
00:29:25,475 --> 00:29:26,985
Son.

190
00:29:27,585 --> 00:29:29,175
Father.

191
00:29:29,355 --> 00:29:31,115
I am here, father.

192
00:29:31,415 --> 00:29:32,765
Son.

193
00:29:38,135 --> 00:29:39,525
Son.

194
00:29:44,535 --> 00:29:46,515
I couldn't protect Gündüz Bey.

195
00:29:49,455 --> 00:29:53,045
Stupid Cerkutay! Stupid Cerkutay!
Stupid Cerkutay!

196
00:29:53,295 --> 00:29:55,145
Don't, Cerkutay! Don't!

197
00:30:02,745 --> 00:30:04,285
Gündüz.

198
00:30:12,575 --> 00:30:14,455
I am here!

199
00:30:14,585 --> 00:30:16,615
I am here, Gündüz Bey!

200
00:31:09,585 --> 00:31:12,341
Hang on, Gündüz. We will take you home.

201
00:31:26,515 --> 00:31:29,075
Take the wounded to the healing tent
first!

202
00:31:29,075 --> 00:31:31,595
Even the enemies. They are still people.

203
00:31:36,455 --> 00:31:38,195
Don't show us mercy!
Kill us!

204
00:31:38,615 --> 00:31:40,635
You took our castle! You can kill us!

205
00:31:41,065 --> 00:31:44,145
We do not persecute those who stand
bravely, even if the enemies.

206
00:31:44,555 --> 00:31:47,115
We have come to hold the oppressors
to account.

207
00:31:47,295 --> 00:31:49,295
And we will.

208
00:31:49,615 --> 00:31:52,455
My Osman Bey will find that dog Nikola.

209
00:31:52,835 --> 00:31:54,915
You are our prisoners now.

210
00:31:55,635 --> 00:31:59,035
But know that as long as you are not
hostile to us...

211
00:31:59,295 --> 00:32:01,855
...you will see nothing from us but mercy.

212
00:32:05,175 --> 00:32:06,695
Take the prisoners.

213
00:32:19,175 --> 00:32:20,995
Nikola must have set a trap.

214
00:32:20,995 --> 00:32:23,775
-Be careful.
-As you order, my Bey!

215
00:32:45,235 --> 00:32:46,595
Come on, my Orhan.

216
00:32:46,975 --> 00:32:48,495
Come on, my Shahzada.

217
00:32:48,875 --> 00:32:51,615
You must have left a trace behind you.

218
00:32:54,585 --> 00:32:57,725
There is no trace of him. What do we do
now?

219
00:32:59,585 --> 00:33:02,645
Don't worry. We surely will find
something.

220
00:33:04,145 --> 00:33:06,665
Don't worry, sister.

221
00:33:06,805 --> 00:33:08,845
We will save our Orhan.

222
00:33:09,325 --> 00:33:12,285
I hope so, sister. I hope so.

223
00:33:22,705 --> 00:33:24,725
Malhun Hatun! Bala Hatun!

224
00:33:33,605 --> 00:33:37,165
They obviously stayed the night here.

225
00:33:47,105 --> 00:33:48,825
The traces go this way.

226
00:34:01,345 --> 00:34:02,725
Hatuns!

227
00:34:03,525 --> 00:34:04,905
There is another trace.

228
00:34:07,525 --> 00:34:09,344
They may have gone this way too.

229
00:34:10,685 --> 00:34:12,364
Do you think they separated?

230
00:34:12,645 --> 00:34:14,025
Or...

231
00:34:14,905 --> 00:34:16,725
...do they want to deceive us?

232
00:34:19,505 --> 00:34:21,324
Who are these people, Bala?

233
00:34:23,324 --> 00:34:25,625
It is my mistake.

234
00:34:25,784 --> 00:34:28,045
I gave Holofira to the soldiers just like
that.

235
00:34:28,445 --> 00:34:31,485
How would you even know, sister?

236
00:34:32,844 --> 00:34:35,685
We were deceived by their disguise.
We couldn't have known.

237
00:34:39,784 --> 00:34:42,304
You never know what these dogs will do.

238
00:34:42,585 --> 00:34:44,405
We musth search both ways.

239
00:34:44,925 --> 00:34:47,264
Let's separate into two and search then.

240
00:34:47,784 --> 00:34:50,545
You are right, Bala Hatun.
This is the best way.

241
00:34:51,585 --> 00:34:53,344
Alps! Come with me.

242
00:34:53,844 --> 00:34:56,364
Come on, sisters! This way!

243
00:35:07,125 --> 00:35:10,125
It is hard to go on foot. We need horses.

244
00:35:10,245 --> 00:35:11,965
Don't think about horses.

245
00:35:12,905 --> 00:35:16,405
First, we have to find somewhere to hide
these kids.

246
00:35:17,225 --> 00:35:19,005
Caves?

247
00:35:19,405 --> 00:35:23,265
Osman knows the caves like the back of
his hand. No way.

248
00:35:24,165 --> 00:35:28,245
Let's take a breath. Then we will go to
Master Arius' secret place.

249
00:35:35,045 --> 00:35:36,605
Holofira...

250
00:35:37,225 --> 00:35:39,285
...that necklace was very important to
you.

251
00:35:39,365 --> 00:35:40,645
Why?

252
00:35:40,645 --> 00:35:44,005
I wanted to leave it to you as a memory.

253
00:35:44,565 --> 00:35:47,365
I know you will take good care of it
as well as I do.

254
00:35:49,785 --> 00:35:52,845
Of course, I will. What is important to
you is important to me.

255
00:35:54,285 --> 00:35:56,565
But I must give you something as well.

256
00:35:58,645 --> 00:36:00,805
You can if we can survive this.

257
00:36:02,365 --> 00:36:04,185
We will, I hope.

258
00:36:04,605 --> 00:36:07,145
My mother and father won't leave us here.

259
00:36:20,085 --> 00:36:22,105
Can you reach it?

260
00:36:22,405 --> 00:36:25,185
The dagger. Can you take it?

261
00:37:37,325 --> 00:37:39,085
Damn it! They are escaping!

262
00:38:15,445 --> 00:38:16,965
Hang on.

263
00:38:18,445 --> 00:38:21,265
Take this. Put this on your wound.

264
00:38:22,965 --> 00:38:24,945
Wait here.

265
00:38:26,085 --> 00:38:29,965
What will heal us is the death of Nikola,
my Bey.

266
00:38:30,605 --> 00:38:32,825
We will take care of ourselves.

267
00:38:35,165 --> 00:38:36,705
Thank you.

268
00:38:37,165 --> 00:38:38,705
Stay here.

269
00:38:39,025 --> 00:38:42,585
Hang on. Hang on, valiants!

270
00:38:55,365 --> 00:38:57,105
There are traces here!

271
00:39:07,925 --> 00:39:09,705
This charcoal trail.

272
00:39:32,665 --> 00:39:34,185
Baysungur!

273
00:39:34,705 --> 00:39:36,725
This is the second charcoal trail we see.

274
00:39:36,725 --> 00:39:38,585
This may be from Orhan.

275
00:39:38,585 --> 00:39:40,345
Right, Bala Hatun.

276
00:39:40,425 --> 00:39:41,985
The traces increase as we go on.

277
00:39:42,065 --> 00:39:44,565
These traces must be from my Shahzada.

278
00:39:44,805 --> 00:39:47,845
My smart boy! He knows we will go after
him!

279
00:39:48,025 --> 00:39:49,385
Come on!

280
00:39:49,465 --> 00:39:51,485
We are on the right path, thankfully.

281
00:39:51,505 --> 00:39:54,565
We will find our Shahzada, sister!
Only a little is left!

282
00:39:55,085 --> 00:39:57,125
We will, sister. We will.

283
00:40:14,425 --> 00:40:16,205
There is trace here too!

284
00:40:20,345 --> 00:40:21,885
Hang on, son.

285
00:40:22,185 --> 00:40:24,425
Your mother's going to save you.

286
00:40:24,425 --> 00:40:26,145
Let's go! Get a move on!

287
00:41:03,885 --> 00:41:05,945
Come, Osman Bey.

288
00:41:06,505 --> 00:41:07,845
Come.

289
00:41:31,945 --> 00:41:34,005
For God's sake, Osman Bey.

290
00:41:34,605 --> 00:41:38,145
Do you think I'm the type of guy to...

291
00:41:38,865 --> 00:41:41,405
...take some gold and flee his castle?

292
00:41:46,885 --> 00:41:48,645
I'm not that guy.

293
00:41:50,005 --> 00:41:52,185
I got two devotions:...

294
00:41:52,685 --> 00:41:54,385
...one of them is Rome,...

295
00:41:55,185 --> 00:41:58,065
...the other is the revenge
I'll get from you.

296
00:41:59,325 --> 00:42:00,905
Revenge, huh?

297
00:42:04,085 --> 00:42:05,405
Good.

298
00:42:07,385 --> 00:42:09,125
I am right in front of you.

299
00:42:12,805 --> 00:42:14,885
This is the time to get revenge.

300
00:42:15,065 --> 00:42:16,885
I already lost my castle.

301
00:42:17,745 --> 00:42:21,925
But you didn't win a whole lot either.

302
00:42:24,245 --> 00:42:25,905
I took İnegöl.

303
00:42:29,645 --> 00:42:31,085
So,...

304
00:42:33,225 --> 00:42:34,965
...your life is next.

305
00:42:35,025 --> 00:42:37,095
I took a lot from you as well, Osman Bey.

306
00:42:37,185 --> 00:42:39,305
I took your loved ones away from you.

307
00:42:39,485 --> 00:42:41,665
Do you remember your brother?

308
00:42:41,765 --> 00:42:45,495
I gave you a promise when those two
senile old men were on the throne for...

309
00:42:45,495 --> 00:42:47,025
...Sultanship and emperorship.

310
00:42:47,125 --> 00:42:49,765
I said that I was going to
kill you with my bare hands.

311
00:42:50,125 --> 00:42:54,185
I always keep my promises,...

312
00:42:54,345 --> 00:42:56,085
...Osman Bey.

313
00:43:36,225 --> 00:43:37,585
Come at me.

314
00:43:44,325 --> 00:43:45,665
Come at me.

315
00:44:07,885 --> 00:44:10,605
We're running towards
the way we came from.

316
00:44:10,645 --> 00:44:12,165
I put tracks behind us...

317
00:44:12,165 --> 00:44:13,965
...they'll find us eventually.

318
00:44:17,385 --> 00:44:18,965
Let's go.

319
00:44:53,725 --> 00:44:55,545
You're very smart, Orhan.

320
00:44:55,945 --> 00:44:57,805
Come on, keep running.

321
00:44:58,065 --> 00:45:00,145
My brother must have sent help.

322
00:45:06,705 --> 00:45:07,985
Hide behind me.

323
00:45:17,985 --> 00:45:21,405
I told you before not to
dare to escape again.

324
00:45:22,225 --> 00:45:24,575
I'm not going to waste my
energy with you again.

325
00:45:24,985 --> 00:45:26,205
Kill them.

326
00:45:32,125 --> 00:45:33,685
We're here son!

327
00:45:36,305 --> 00:45:38,345
I told you they were going to save us.

328
00:45:38,585 --> 00:45:39,665
Damn it!

329
00:45:48,345 --> 00:45:50,345
My brave son!

330
00:45:52,345 --> 00:45:53,885
My beautiful girl.

331
00:45:54,005 --> 00:45:55,805
Are you guys alright?

332
00:45:59,325 --> 00:46:01,345
We knew you would come, mother.

333
00:46:01,605 --> 00:46:04,445
Thank goodness, my son! Thank goodness!

334
00:46:04,785 --> 00:46:06,305
Thank goodness!

335
00:46:08,285 --> 00:46:12,665
You couldn't even take care
of a couple of kids, you fools!

336
00:46:14,165 --> 00:46:15,725
That's why...

337
00:46:16,425 --> 00:46:19,515
...you've got to be careful when
you choose the men beside you.

338
00:46:20,145 --> 00:46:22,985
Kids getting shot is not good at all.

339
00:46:23,745 --> 00:46:25,805
So, Barkın Bey...

340
00:46:26,525 --> 00:46:28,525
...it fell to my lot once again.

341
00:46:29,385 --> 00:46:30,925
My Orhan.

342
00:46:33,425 --> 00:46:35,705
Thank goodness!

343
00:46:35,705 --> 00:46:37,725
You weren't scrared much, right?

344
00:46:37,905 --> 00:46:39,625
We were scared at first.

345
00:46:39,705 --> 00:46:42,085
But then, we believed that you would come.

346
00:46:43,695 --> 00:46:45,325
Orhan made me believe it.

347
00:46:46,465 --> 00:46:49,265
Praise be, my valiant prince!

348
00:46:50,005 --> 00:46:53,065
I knew you wouldn't let us down.

349
00:46:54,405 --> 00:46:55,935
My smart boy.

350
00:48:50,525 --> 00:48:52,025
Nikola.

351
00:48:56,835 --> 00:49:02,925
Today, only my promise will be kept.

352
00:49:09,695 --> 00:49:11,205
You,...

353
00:49:14,405 --> 00:49:17,135
...you attacked my lineage.

354
00:49:20,295 --> 00:49:24,885
You, you attacked my lineage.

355
00:49:24,985 --> 00:49:26,985
Come here!

356
00:49:26,985 --> 00:49:30,265
You attacked my religion.

357
00:49:30,265 --> 00:49:31,665
Come!

358
00:49:31,665 --> 00:49:35,495
You attacked my tribe.

359
00:49:36,985 --> 00:49:38,205
Come!

360
00:49:38,205 --> 00:49:42,155
You spilled the blood of my loved ones.

361
00:49:47,405 --> 00:49:49,005
Come here!

362
00:49:49,005 --> 00:49:50,355
You,...

363
00:49:51,065 --> 00:49:52,385
...you...

364
00:49:52,695 --> 00:50:01,225
...you can take nothing from me, Nikola.

365
00:50:01,835 --> 00:50:05,985
I will get rid of you.

366
00:50:08,155 --> 00:50:10,865
But, you won't get rid of me easily.

367
00:50:12,355 --> 00:50:15,435
You won't get rid of me easily.

368
00:50:19,205 --> 00:50:21,095
I took İnegöl from you.

369
00:50:21,755 --> 00:50:23,235
İnegöl...

370
00:50:23,835 --> 00:50:28,065
...İnegöl belongs to Turks, from now on.

371
00:50:29,235 --> 00:50:34,955
And I planted the flag of Islam
in the middle of İnegöl.

372
00:50:45,095 --> 00:50:50,665
Osman in the castle, and his hatuns
and children will die in the forest.

373
00:50:52,495 --> 00:50:53,665
Listen to me...

374
00:50:55,755 --> 00:50:58,615
...look at those dead soldiers
on the ground very carefully.

375
00:51:00,495 --> 00:51:02,955
If any of you make one mistake...

376
00:51:03,695 --> 00:51:05,665
...you will end up the same way as them.

377
00:51:05,795 --> 00:51:07,335
My Orhan,...

378
00:51:07,335 --> 00:51:08,905
...whose dogs are these?

379
00:51:08,905 --> 00:51:10,905
Did they say anything?

380
00:51:12,435 --> 00:51:14,195
No, Mother Bala.

381
00:51:15,695 --> 00:51:18,225
But there was another guy leading them.

382
00:51:18,695 --> 00:51:20,735
He fleed once you guys arrived.

383
00:51:24,265 --> 00:51:27,095
You saved Kaya alps from getting poisoned.

384
00:51:27,295 --> 00:51:29,325
Praise be, you brave kids!

385
00:51:30,695 --> 00:51:33,065
That was Fira's talent, aunt Selvi.

386
00:51:36,185 --> 00:51:38,185
If she didn't send the word...

387
00:51:39,205 --> 00:51:40,785
...Allah for bid.

388
00:51:43,355 --> 00:51:44,935
Thank goodness!

389
00:51:47,495 --> 00:51:48,805
The bow.

390
00:52:17,835 --> 00:52:19,365
Protect them!

391
00:52:22,835 --> 00:52:24,365
- Bala!
- Bala!

392
00:52:24,525 --> 00:52:26,805
Watch over yourselves!

393
00:52:26,805 --> 00:52:28,805
Protect the kids.

394
00:52:29,185 --> 00:52:30,465
Bala, are you alright?

395
00:52:30,465 --> 00:52:32,465
I am alright.

396
00:52:34,695 --> 00:52:36,265
Hatuns.

397
00:52:40,325 --> 00:52:41,865
Barkın Bey.

398
00:52:42,295 --> 00:52:43,825
Barkın?

399
00:52:50,785 --> 00:52:52,665
Are you guys well?

400
00:52:53,325 --> 00:52:55,155
We're well, thank goodness.

401
00:52:55,285 --> 00:52:57,055
The scoundrel was hiding.

402
00:52:57,055 --> 00:52:58,805
But we took care of him.

403
00:52:58,805 --> 00:53:00,805
Thank you, Barkın Bey.

404
00:53:00,805 --> 00:53:02,805
You arrived just in time.

405
00:53:10,495 --> 00:53:13,535
Kill all of them besides Selvi, but...

406
00:53:14,865 --> 00:53:19,155
...I'll kill anyone who even
touches the hair of Selvi.

407
00:53:20,665 --> 00:53:22,025
Come on.

408
00:53:25,405 --> 00:53:27,165
My bey, İnegöl...

409
00:53:27,895 --> 00:53:29,895
...Osman Bey took it.

410
00:53:30,635 --> 00:53:32,155
Damn it!

411
00:53:33,955 --> 00:53:35,525
God damn it!

412
00:53:41,585 --> 00:53:44,085
I got good news.

413
00:53:44,495 --> 00:53:46,495
We got word from alps...

414
00:53:47,555 --> 00:53:49,255
...Osman Bey,...

415
00:53:50,015 --> 00:53:53,085
...Osman Bey has conquered İnegöl.

416
00:53:54,685 --> 00:53:56,895
Praise be, my Osman Bey!

417
00:53:56,895 --> 00:54:01,075
Thank goodness!

418
00:54:02,275 --> 00:54:04,775
Thank for the good news, Barkın!

419
00:54:08,075 --> 00:54:10,595
Bala, we should take care of your wound.

420
00:54:11,355 --> 00:54:14,475
Let's get it done quickly
so that we can go to İnegöl.

421
00:54:14,815 --> 00:54:17,875
Alahattin probably sent the word,
Osman Bey must be worried.

422
00:54:18,525 --> 00:54:21,275
Alps, start a fire!

423
00:54:21,275 --> 00:54:23,275
Come on!

424
00:56:02,845 --> 00:56:04,385
He's got a lot of fractures.

425
00:56:04,385 --> 00:56:06,385
We're going to have to open his skin.

426
00:56:06,825 --> 00:56:09,045
Let's do whatever we
have to do, Kumral Abdal.

427
00:56:09,045 --> 00:56:10,385
Tell me,...

428
00:56:10,385 --> 00:56:11,985
...what should I go gather?

429
00:56:11,985 --> 00:56:13,985
We did whatever we could for now.

430
00:56:14,645 --> 00:56:15,985
We will pray.

431
00:56:18,215 --> 00:56:20,325
His wounds will heal...

432
00:56:21,215 --> 00:56:23,275
...and he'll be alright, if Allah permits.

433
00:56:23,645 --> 00:56:25,195
If Allah permits.

434
00:56:27,475 --> 00:56:28,995
My father.

435
00:56:33,815 --> 00:56:35,825
We just got reunited, father.

436
00:56:37,615 --> 00:56:39,185
You'll be well.

437
00:56:43,125 --> 00:56:45,215
Don't go this early.

438
00:56:46,185 --> 00:56:47,975
Don't go father.

439
00:56:51,955 --> 00:56:53,485
Temur,...

440
00:56:53,585 --> 00:56:56,155
...your father's a strong, tough man.

441
00:56:56,155 --> 00:56:57,675
He'll recover,...

442
00:56:57,675 --> 00:56:58,755
...if Allah permits.

443
00:56:58,755 --> 00:57:00,355
You stay strong.

444
00:57:00,355 --> 00:57:02,355
Be tough.

445
00:57:05,045 --> 00:57:08,615
He is the great Gündüz Bey.

446
00:57:09,585 --> 00:57:12,155
He is too tough for a couple of fractures.

447
00:57:12,725 --> 00:57:14,815
He will be well, if Allah permits.

448
00:57:18,525 --> 00:57:21,095
Right, Kumral Abdal?

449
00:57:22,185 --> 00:57:24,255
If Allah permits.

450
00:57:25,185 --> 00:57:26,695
If Allah permits.

451
00:57:34,955 --> 00:57:38,045
Orhan and the hatuns are
in trouble right now.

452
00:57:38,045 --> 00:57:40,995
They used the conquest as an
opportunity, those damn demons!

453
00:57:41,755 --> 00:57:43,515
Don't you have any worry, my valiant.

454
00:57:43,725 --> 00:57:46,975
Both your brother and mother
will come back without a scratch.

455
00:57:50,045 --> 00:57:51,595
Look me in the eyes.

456
00:57:51,645 --> 00:57:52,995
They will.

457
00:57:54,275 --> 00:57:56,115
Thank Allah, I have no worries.

458
00:57:56,785 --> 00:57:59,295
My father taught us how
to get out of any trouble.

459
00:57:59,455 --> 00:58:01,245
Praise be, my valiant!

460
00:58:01,245 --> 00:58:02,755
Praise be!

461
00:58:03,185 --> 00:58:05,185
My brave valiant.

462
00:58:05,225 --> 00:58:06,815
Praise be!

463
00:58:06,895 --> 00:58:09,955
With enough effort, Allah gives aid.

464
00:58:11,125 --> 00:58:12,555
We'll go after them.

465
00:58:13,295 --> 00:58:15,295
Osman Bey is coming!

466
00:58:34,955 --> 00:59:07,045
- Long live, Osman Bey!
- Long live, Osman Bey!

467
00:59:07,045 --> 00:59:11,475
- Allahu Akbar!
- Allahu Akbar!

468
00:59:11,785 --> 00:59:14,495
How are we going to exlpain
it to our Bey, Turgut Bey?

469
00:59:14,495 --> 00:59:17,625
Gündüz Bey in one side,
Orhan is in the other.

470
00:59:18,295 --> 00:59:20,335
He will know, Boran.

471
00:59:20,665 --> 00:59:22,465
He will know the truth.

472
00:59:31,435 --> 00:59:33,005
Son.

473
00:59:35,095 --> 00:59:36,435
Come on.

474
00:59:42,765 --> 00:59:44,495
Take him to the dungeon.

475
00:59:44,495 --> 00:59:46,495
Yes, my bey!

476
00:59:46,495 --> 00:59:48,495
I know the way.

477
00:59:52,125 --> 00:59:53,705
Nikola

478
00:59:58,695 --> 01:00:00,195
Alaattin.

479
01:00:00,295 --> 01:00:02,295
Son, what are you doing here?

480
01:00:09,605 --> 01:00:10,985
Tell me.

481
01:00:12,955 --> 01:00:15,205
Bless your victories, Osman Bey!

482
01:00:17,955 --> 01:00:19,955
We came to witness your victory, father.

483
01:00:21,185 --> 01:00:23,065
Praise be!

484
01:00:23,635 --> 01:00:25,165
Hatuns.

485
01:00:30,695 --> 01:00:33,005
Bala, are you well?

486
01:00:33,005 --> 01:00:35,005
It's no big deal, I'm well.

487
01:00:35,965 --> 01:00:37,695
Everlasting victories, my bey!

488
01:00:37,695 --> 01:00:39,695
Thank you all!

489
01:00:56,725 --> 01:00:58,265
Kids.

490
01:00:59,325 --> 01:01:00,835
Kids.

491
01:01:03,895 --> 01:01:05,435
Turgut Bey.

492
01:01:08,405 --> 01:01:10,165
I saw everyone.

493
01:01:12,185 --> 01:01:14,035
But I couldn't see my brother.

494
01:01:14,725 --> 01:01:16,605
I couldn't see Aktemur.

495
01:01:16,605 --> 01:01:18,605
Where are they?

496
01:01:24,265 --> 01:01:26,355
Gündüz Bey is not well.

497
01:01:29,955 --> 01:01:31,995
He's wounded badly, Osman Bey.

498
01:01:32,635 --> 01:01:34,635
What are you saying?

499
01:01:42,895 --> 01:01:44,455
Where is he?

500
01:02:04,585 --> 01:02:07,285
HARMANKAYA CASTLE

501
01:02:08,650 --> 01:02:09,990
Father,...

502
01:02:13,210 --> 01:02:15,750
...son and the holy spirit.

503
01:02:17,110 --> 01:02:18,470
God.

504
01:02:19,590 --> 01:02:21,150
Son of God,...

505
01:02:21,990 --> 01:02:23,510
...and the holy spirit.

506
01:02:25,010 --> 01:02:26,730
How could...

507
01:02:29,190 --> 01:02:31,210
...three deities be one?

508
01:02:31,770 --> 01:02:33,110
How?

509
01:02:34,090 --> 01:02:35,810
How could they be one?

510
01:02:47,930 --> 01:02:50,150
There is no,...

511
01:02:54,150 --> 01:02:56,930
...other deity.

512
01:02:59,450 --> 01:03:01,510
There is no other God.

513
01:03:04,150 --> 01:03:05,930
The only deity...

514
01:03:07,030 --> 01:03:08,450
...is Allah.

515
01:03:10,990 --> 01:03:12,550
The only deity...

516
01:03:15,190 --> 01:03:18,630
...is Allah and nothing else.

517
01:03:21,990 --> 01:03:24,150
Only Allah.

518
01:03:28,410 --> 01:03:30,110
Only Allah.

519
01:03:31,690 --> 01:03:33,010
Allah...

520
01:03:33,350 --> 01:03:34,870
...is the...

521
01:03:35,710 --> 01:03:37,730
...greatest.

522
01:03:42,630 --> 01:03:46,610
Sir, Commander Romanos is
here, and would like to see you.

523
01:03:50,690 --> 01:03:52,070
Let him come in.

524
01:03:52,770 --> 01:03:55,890
Let's not make the greatest commander
of Rome wait any longer.

525
01:04:12,630 --> 01:04:16,470
Osman has played a big trick on us.
A very big one.

526
01:04:20,150 --> 01:04:21,830
They have infitraded us.

527
01:04:22,150 --> 01:04:25,490
İnegöl is in the dirty hands of Osman,
do you understand that, Kosses?

528
01:04:25,970 --> 01:04:27,550
This is an insult to Rome!

529
01:04:29,550 --> 01:04:31,130
Osman,...

530
01:04:32,390 --> 01:04:33,910
...damn you!

531
01:04:35,090 --> 01:04:38,150
What happens in Rome
stays in Rome, Romanos.

532
01:04:38,250 --> 01:04:40,250
You know that better than anyone.

533
01:04:46,430 --> 01:04:49,250
I know one other thing, Kosses.

534
01:04:50,950 --> 01:04:53,990
If you hadn't gone soft
on Osman this much...

535
01:04:55,250 --> 01:04:57,290
...if you weren't friendly towards him,...

536
01:04:57,650 --> 01:04:59,510
...he was already destroyed.

537
01:04:59,910 --> 01:05:02,150
Everything was an act.

538
01:05:02,450 --> 01:05:04,830
We grew up together.

539
01:05:05,030 --> 01:05:07,410
You know me best, Romanos.

540
01:05:07,710 --> 01:05:12,070
A handful of lords could
not defeat one goatherd!

541
01:05:12,190 --> 01:05:14,070
You smeared Rome with your greed.

542
01:05:14,190 --> 01:05:16,290
You became friends with your enemies!

543
01:05:16,630 --> 01:05:21,450
You know that I would never be friends
with a Turk witout an ulterior motive.

544
01:05:26,310 --> 01:05:27,630
Then,...

545
01:05:28,330 --> 01:05:32,390
...to show your ulterior motives
don't conflict with Rome's interests...

546
01:05:34,290 --> 01:05:36,350
...you will solve this problem Kosses.

547
01:05:37,210 --> 01:05:38,770
I will.

548
01:05:39,330 --> 01:05:40,910
Don't worry.

549
01:05:41,610 --> 01:05:45,690
Be we need to act carefully, brother.

550
01:05:46,970 --> 01:05:51,610
If we underestimate Osman now,
we would show weakness.

551
01:05:52,130 --> 01:05:54,370
Osman is a dangereous man.

552
01:05:55,490 --> 01:05:56,990
We are...

553
01:05:59,370 --> 01:06:01,630
...more dangereous, of course.

554
01:06:02,110 --> 01:06:04,170
And we will show him that.

555
01:06:09,990 --> 01:06:14,430
With your methods, or with
mine, it doesn't matter.

556
01:06:17,410 --> 01:06:18,990
Sword,...

557
01:06:21,350 --> 01:06:22,870
...or games.

558
01:06:23,430 --> 01:06:25,650
Whatever it costs...

559
01:06:26,790 --> 01:06:29,370
...we are going to take İnegöl from Osman.

560
01:06:30,970 --> 01:06:34,530
Ambassador of the emperor
was on his way to stop the war.

561
01:06:35,210 --> 01:06:36,990
He's about to be here, probably.

562
01:06:37,330 --> 01:06:40,050
Hide your sword for now, Romanos.

563
01:06:40,270 --> 01:06:42,750
We will defeat him with my methods.

564
01:06:43,350 --> 01:06:45,050
Game against game.

565
01:06:47,850 --> 01:06:49,870
What's on your mind, Kosses?

566
01:06:50,350 --> 01:06:53,210
Let's welcome the ambassador
of the emperor first,...

567
01:06:53,830 --> 01:06:55,630
...we'll talk about that later.

568
01:07:29,330 --> 01:07:30,910
He's opening his eyes.

569
01:07:30,970 --> 01:07:32,470
My father's opening his eyes.

570
01:07:32,470 --> 01:07:33,690
Gündüz?

571
01:07:36,650 --> 01:07:38,230
Gündüz.

572
01:07:39,070 --> 01:07:41,090
Thank Allah!

573
01:07:42,770 --> 01:07:45,770
I told you, he is the great Gündüz Bey.

574
01:07:46,630 --> 01:07:48,650
He is going to conquer many castles.

575
01:07:48,990 --> 01:07:50,990
He doen't die easily.

576
01:07:57,270 --> 01:07:58,790
Ayşe.

577
01:07:59,010 --> 01:08:00,590
My Gündüz.

578
01:08:09,870 --> 01:08:11,210
Son.

579
01:08:11,570 --> 01:08:12,890
My father.

580
01:08:14,350 --> 01:08:16,149
Did we take İnegöl?

581
01:08:17,109 --> 01:08:18,649
We did father.

582
01:08:18,649 --> 01:08:20,649
Thanks to you.

583
01:08:21,069 --> 01:08:22,649
Thank Allah!

584
01:08:22,850 --> 01:08:24,410
Thanks to Allah!

585
01:08:24,729 --> 01:08:26,510
Ayşe, see?

586
01:08:27,770 --> 01:08:29,490
We took İnegöl.

587
01:08:31,770 --> 01:08:34,770
Our son is with us alive and well.

588
01:08:39,290 --> 01:08:41,430
Even if I die, I'll die happy.

589
01:08:42,229 --> 01:08:44,069
Don't say that my bey.

590
01:08:44,810 --> 01:08:48,550
We're yet to see the good
deeds ours son will accomplish.

591
01:08:57,890 --> 01:08:59,470
Brother.

592
01:09:06,990 --> 01:09:08,529
Brother.

593
01:09:09,770 --> 01:09:11,310
Are you well?

594
01:09:12,109 --> 01:09:13,649
My bey,...

595
01:09:15,189 --> 01:09:17,270
...he's got a lot of fractures.

596
01:09:30,370 --> 01:09:31,950
I am well.

597
01:09:32,550 --> 01:09:34,350
I am well, brother.

598
01:09:35,649 --> 01:09:38,170
My brother just coquered İnegöl.

599
01:09:38,290 --> 01:09:40,149
How could I not be well?

600
01:09:40,290 --> 01:09:41,790
I'm well.

601
01:09:41,790 --> 01:09:43,510
That's right, brother.

602
01:09:44,330 --> 01:09:46,069
We have conquered İnegöl

603
01:09:46,950 --> 01:09:48,710
It's ours now.

604
01:09:49,270 --> 01:09:50,810
Thank goodness!

605
01:10:06,250 --> 01:10:07,750
Kumral Abdal?

606
01:10:08,970 --> 01:10:10,510
How is he?

607
01:10:12,950 --> 01:10:15,510
He'll be well, if Allah permits, my bey.

608
01:10:23,630 --> 01:10:26,170
You know the trust I have in you.

609
01:10:27,730 --> 01:10:29,570
My brother is in your hands.

610
01:10:32,670 --> 01:10:35,750
Brother, you rest for now.

611
01:10:36,370 --> 01:10:37,950
I'll come back again.

612
01:10:39,990 --> 01:10:41,310
May Allah bless you!

613
01:11:09,990 --> 01:11:12,050
Get well soon, Gündüz Bey!

614
01:11:14,330 --> 01:11:16,390
May Allah give you healing, Gündüz Bey!

615
01:11:16,550 --> 01:11:18,650
You'll be alright soon, if Allah permits.

616
01:11:32,950 --> 01:11:34,970
- Boran.
- My Bey?

617
01:11:35,630 --> 01:11:38,170
We'll do the treatment of the alps here.

618
01:11:39,050 --> 01:11:42,550
We'll stay in this castle
until my brother can walk

619
01:11:43,090 --> 01:11:44,550
I am at your command, my bey!

620
01:11:46,810 --> 01:11:48,250
Let's go.

621
01:13:08,690 --> 01:13:12,070
Allahu Akbar Allahu Akabar

622
01:13:13,450 --> 01:13:21,530
Allahu Akbar Allahu Akabar

623
01:13:22,650 --> 01:13:34,450
I am a witness that there
are no other Gods than Allah!

624
01:13:36,450 --> 01:13:49,950
I am a witness that there
are no other Gods than Allah!

625
01:13:53,310 --> 01:14:02,850
And I am a witness that Muhammad
is the messenger of Allah!

626
01:14:05,170 --> 01:14:07,930
Rome is the greatest.
Rome is the greatest!

627
01:14:08,390 --> 01:14:10,090
Ceasar is the greatest!

628
01:14:10,490 --> 01:14:12,190
Rome is the greatest!

629
01:14:12,190 --> 01:14:21,710
And I am a witness that Muhammad
is the messenger of Allah!

630
01:14:24,730 --> 01:14:30,750
Rome is the greatest,
Ceasar is the greatest!

631
01:14:30,750 --> 01:14:33,330
Aya Nikola is the greatest!

632
01:14:33,330 --> 01:14:45,410
Hayyal Es Salah!

633
01:14:46,750 --> 01:14:53,330
Hayyalel Felah!

634
01:14:54,790 --> 01:15:04,368
Hayyalel Felah!

635
01:19:03,250 --> 01:19:06,270
The Great Allah,...

636
01:19:07,450 --> 01:19:10,270
...you are the one who sent the book...

637
01:19:10,610 --> 01:19:13,350
...you are the one who
makes the clouds move...

638
01:19:14,050 --> 01:19:18,110
...you are the wisest.

639
01:19:18,650 --> 01:19:20,210
My dear Allah,...

640
01:19:21,500 --> 01:19:27,260
...you are the one who helped
us with defeating our enemies.

641
01:19:27,930 --> 01:19:32,970
May you protect us against
the enemies at all times!

642
01:19:33,030 --> 01:19:34,350
- Amen!
- Amen!

643
01:19:34,350 --> 01:19:39,730
May you grant us with victory
against our enemies, Great Allah!

644
01:19:39,730 --> 01:19:41,230
- Amen!
- Amen!

645
01:19:41,230 --> 01:19:44,040
May you never allow them to
suppress our azans, dear Allah.

646
01:19:44,040 --> 01:19:45,390
- Amen!
- Amen!

647
01:19:45,390 --> 01:19:48,590
May you never allow them to
lift down our flags, dear Allah!

648
01:19:48,590 --> 01:19:49,810
- Amen!
- Amen!

649
01:19:49,810 --> 01:19:51,810
Amen, dear Allah!

650
01:19:52,630 --> 01:19:55,370
Accept our prayers.

651
01:20:02,485 --> 01:20:04,985
The İnegöl folk,...

652
01:20:07,485 --> 01:20:08,985
...İnegöl...

653
01:20:09,345 --> 01:20:11,365
...is the land of the Turks, from now on.

654
01:20:13,545 --> 01:20:14,845
But,...

655
01:20:15,205 --> 01:20:17,745
...don't ever be pessimistic.

656
01:20:18,465 --> 01:20:22,665
We did not come here to be your enemies.

657
01:20:23,645 --> 01:20:28,185
We did not come here to oppress.

658
01:20:29,045 --> 01:20:32,605
In hour home, there is only prosperity,...

659
01:20:33,205 --> 01:20:34,705
...and peace.

660
01:20:35,645 --> 01:20:37,025
That's why...

661
01:20:37,765 --> 01:20:40,565
...all of you can get back to your trade.

662
01:20:41,125 --> 01:20:44,965
And never abandon farming.

663
01:20:46,585 --> 01:20:48,145
Your rights,...

664
01:20:49,045 --> 01:20:50,605
...lives,...

665
01:20:50,705 --> 01:20:52,205
...and freedom...

666
01:20:53,885 --> 01:20:55,665
...is in our hands.

667
01:21:09,505 --> 01:21:11,085
What do you want?

668
01:21:14,340 --> 01:21:16,970
We were going to come
to this castle like this, Kosses?

669
01:21:17,140 --> 01:21:19,700
Time is running out, Romanos.

670
01:21:20,120 --> 01:21:22,180
Tell your bey we're here.

671
01:21:22,900 --> 01:21:25,140
Tell him we've got someone
important with us.

672
01:21:36,440 --> 01:21:38,000
Tell your bey of yours...

673
01:21:38,300 --> 01:21:40,880
...that the ambassador
of emperor Andronikos...

674
01:21:41,100 --> 01:21:42,620
...himself...

675
01:21:42,620 --> 01:21:44,620
...is here.

676
01:21:45,440 --> 01:21:47,140
Ambassador Alkiz is here.

677
01:21:59,820 --> 01:22:04,000
Devastation will occur
in battle, of course.

678
01:22:04,860 --> 01:22:06,440
The demolished homes,...

679
01:22:06,620 --> 01:22:08,180
...stores,...

680
01:22:08,180 --> 01:22:09,680
...lands,...

681
01:22:10,120 --> 01:22:13,220
...we wouldn't want to
have that effect you.

682
01:22:14,460 --> 01:22:18,340
Therefore, let us know your outages.

683
01:22:18,700 --> 01:22:20,860
We'll compensate for them with interest.

684
01:22:21,160 --> 01:22:25,400
Know that we have seized
the properties of the soldiers,...

685
01:22:25,400 --> 01:22:27,940
...commanders, and the traders...

686
01:22:28,580 --> 01:22:36,900
...who drew their weapons
and shed the blood of my alps.

687
01:22:37,940 --> 01:22:40,480
They will be given to the
veterans as tropies.

688
01:22:40,840 --> 01:22:44,720
And we will help the martyr families.

689
01:22:44,940 --> 01:22:46,720
As I've heard...

690
01:22:46,940 --> 01:22:50,500
...some have fled from İnegöl once
they heard Turks were coming.

691
01:22:51,660 --> 01:22:54,160
Send word to them now,...

692
01:22:54,520 --> 01:22:56,580
...they can get back to their properties.

693
01:22:57,200 --> 01:23:00,220
They can go back to do trade.

694
01:23:00,940 --> 01:23:05,560
And they can worship freely.

695
01:23:05,860 --> 01:23:09,140
In the castle or in the tribe.

696
01:23:09,340 --> 01:23:12,920
We are always with the oppressed.

697
01:23:13,720 --> 01:23:18,820
You are in our hands, from now on.

698
01:23:19,600 --> 01:23:21,120
That is why...

699
01:23:22,760 --> 01:23:25,260
...everyone can get back to work, now.

700
01:23:25,260 --> 01:23:27,060
Go ahead.

701
01:23:32,480 --> 01:23:34,040
Osman Bey,...

702
01:23:34,040 --> 01:23:36,040
...I know you from your father.

703
01:23:36,400 --> 01:23:39,180
My ancestors know your ancestor well, too.

704
01:23:40,000 --> 01:23:42,700
We had always heard of
your fairness and mercy.

705
01:23:43,540 --> 01:23:48,100
And I was sure you would follow the steps
of your ancestors. You didn't mislead me.

706
01:23:48,440 --> 01:23:50,940
I am thankful to you on
the behalf of my people.

707
01:23:50,940 --> 01:23:52,940
I would like you to know of my gratitute.

708
01:23:53,380 --> 01:23:55,880
May Allah bless you, priest!

709
01:23:57,040 --> 01:23:59,300
It is in the tradition of our prophet...

710
01:23:59,300 --> 01:24:04,020
...to live by the book
and treat people...

711
01:24:04,400 --> 01:24:06,900
...with fairness and mercy.

712
01:24:08,520 --> 01:24:11,020
We try our best to follow that path.

713
01:24:11,300 --> 01:24:16,380
Our ancestors were always
respectful of others' religon and lives.

714
01:24:18,580 --> 01:24:20,880
Always be assured...

715
01:24:21,900 --> 01:24:27,600
...that in these lands you will live with
us peacefully for the res of your lives.

716
01:24:27,600 --> 01:24:30,120
Thank you, Osman Bey! Thank you!

717
01:24:30,120 --> 01:24:32,120
May Allah bless you!

718
01:24:32,920 --> 01:24:37,160
My Bey, they have sent an ambassador from
the emperorship and would like to see you.

719
01:24:40,520 --> 01:24:41,900
Let them come in.

720
01:24:46,160 --> 01:24:47,720
That is enough.

721
01:24:52,400 --> 01:24:53,980
Welcome.

722
01:24:54,670 --> 01:24:56,170
Osman Bey,...

723
01:24:56,325 --> 01:25:00,405
...I am the shadow of the emperor
Andronikos, the ambassador Alkiz.

724
01:25:00,645 --> 01:25:02,405
I greet you with respect.

725
01:25:02,665 --> 01:25:04,205
May Allah bless you!

726
01:25:04,205 --> 01:25:06,205
Tell me then,...

727
01:25:06,887 --> 01:25:09,297
...what news have you
brought from your emperor?

728
01:25:10,885 --> 01:25:12,425
To be honest...

729
01:25:12,865 --> 01:25:15,565
...I was on the road to
meet you in your tribe.

730
01:25:18,705 --> 01:25:21,745
But then bad news came and
I learned that you were in İnegöl.

731
01:25:21,745 --> 01:25:23,745
And not as a guest...

732
01:25:23,745 --> 01:25:25,445
...as the owner.

733
01:25:27,965 --> 01:25:30,045
You took İnegöl.

734
01:25:31,245 --> 01:25:32,825
That is true.

735
01:25:33,585 --> 01:25:36,165
The İnegöl that was yours yesterday...

736
01:25:36,885 --> 01:25:38,965
...belongst to Islam today.

737
01:25:41,985 --> 01:25:44,845
Apparently, you're not afraid
of the wrath of our emperor.

738
01:25:45,685 --> 01:25:47,485
It is admirable.

739
01:25:48,345 --> 01:25:51,385
There is no problem that
can't be solved through peace.

740
01:25:55,105 --> 01:25:56,885
Through peace?

741
01:26:00,625 --> 01:26:07,165
With Romanos who kidnapped the unarmed
hatuns who were heading to tableland?

742
01:26:09,065 --> 01:26:10,585
Or with...

743
01:26:13,165 --> 01:26:16,385
...the lords who raided our
wedding and tried to kill us?

744
01:26:17,985 --> 01:26:19,245
Tell me.

745
01:26:19,905 --> 01:26:24,445
The lords did not do all of those things
all by themselves of course, but...

746
01:26:25,525 --> 01:26:26,845
...tell me...

747
01:26:27,165 --> 01:26:29,665
...who are we going to make peace with?

748
01:26:31,865 --> 01:26:37,735
Or with the ambassador of
the emperor who set it all up?

749
01:26:41,325 --> 01:26:42,825
Kosses,...

750
01:26:44,445 --> 01:26:47,235
...I know very well that you
prepared an army against me.

751
01:26:49,465 --> 01:26:54,005
That's why, there will be no peace.

752
01:26:59,605 --> 01:27:01,925
Now, rest very well.

753
01:27:02,425 --> 01:27:04,965
We'll discuss in detail in the evening...

754
01:27:05,645 --> 01:27:07,645
...and tell you about our conditions.

755
01:28:01,675 --> 01:28:04,765
Allahu Akbar.

756
01:28:25,565 --> 01:28:29,095
May peace and the mercy
of Allah be upon you!

757
01:28:29,465 --> 01:28:32,715
May peace and the mercy
of Allah be upon you!

758
01:28:36,055 --> 01:28:38,705
Al Fatiha.

759
01:29:07,595 --> 01:29:09,845
Thank Allah!

760
01:29:13,395 --> 01:29:15,915
Thank Allah!

761
01:29:16,485 --> 01:29:22,985
Thank our Allah for granting us with this
conquest and with standing before him...

762
01:29:22,985 --> 01:29:24,855
...peacefully in the courtyard.

763
01:29:26,055 --> 01:29:28,835
Thank Allah!

764
01:29:33,205 --> 01:29:38,495
He made the earth a masjid for us.

765
01:29:38,825 --> 01:29:50,695
It should be the priorty of all Muslims to
pray to him and state his name everywhere.

766
01:29:52,565 --> 01:30:01,425
The messenger of Allah says that
deeds depend on intentions.

767
01:30:01,755 --> 01:30:10,245
A person who speaks his deeds
is for no good.

768
01:30:10,805 --> 01:30:20,885
There are people who do good deeds
only to show off.

769
01:30:21,015 --> 01:30:27,375
They are worse than those
who do no good deeds.

770
01:30:29,625 --> 01:30:31,675
How, my sheik?

771
01:30:31,845 --> 01:30:35,395
How can they be worse than ones
with no good deeds?

772
01:30:35,745 --> 01:30:40,185
Lying is a greatest sin, Cerkutay.

773
01:30:41,445 --> 01:30:52,975
The one who lies with his heart
has a bad fate.

774
01:30:53,045 --> 01:30:57,445
This is secret shirk.

775
01:30:58,055 --> 01:31:06,325
Our prophet says that they'll be judged
the first when the time comes.

776
01:31:08,785 --> 01:31:11,095
May Allah forbid it, my sheik.

777
01:31:11,515 --> 01:31:14,135
May Allah protect us from
being like that.

778
01:31:14,535 --> 01:31:16,895
But who are they?

779
01:31:17,125 --> 01:31:19,695
How will we stay back from becoming
that?

780
01:31:19,955 --> 01:31:21,475
For example...

781
01:31:21,965 --> 01:31:25,825
the people we know to be fallen
martyrs on the battlefield.

782
01:31:26,015 --> 01:31:39,525
Martyrs. They say that they died for
Allah. They lie.

783
01:31:39,605 --> 01:31:46,175
They only go to the battlefield
for glory.

784
01:31:46,305 --> 01:31:50,325
They give their lives for their desires...

785
01:31:50,485 --> 01:31:53,575
not for their Allah.

786
01:31:53,765 --> 01:31:57,945
They'll be dragged to the ground...

787
01:31:58,325 --> 01:32:00,565
and be sent to hell.

788
01:32:00,985 --> 01:32:05,075
In Allah's place, martyrdom...

789
01:32:05,425 --> 01:32:12,555
is being free of your desires
and fighting for Allah.

790
01:32:16,695 --> 01:32:24,365
The other are those who learn science
and religion. Who teaches it.

791
01:32:24,715 --> 01:32:29,785
They don't do it for Allah.

792
01:32:30,795 --> 01:32:36,215
But only to be known as scholars.

793
01:32:36,355 --> 01:32:43,375
They only read Qur-an to be acknowledged
by others.

794
01:32:44,635 --> 01:32:51,155
They will also be dragged to hell.

795
01:32:51,785 --> 01:32:54,075
The third is...

796
01:32:54,285 --> 01:33:04,385
the ones who were destined with
great wealth.

797
01:33:05,535 --> 01:33:08,925
When they are asked what they
did Allah...

798
01:33:09,185 --> 01:33:18,645
they say that they shared their
money with the ones in need.

799
01:33:20,305 --> 01:33:31,365
But Allah knows hearts and
sees the truth.

800
01:33:32,305 --> 01:33:39,765
They shared their wealth to be known
as generous, not for Allah.

801
01:33:41,305 --> 01:33:50,025
Those people will also get dragged
to hell.

802
01:33:50,255 --> 01:33:53,605
May Allah forbid.

803
01:33:57,315 --> 01:34:05,435
Hypocrisy is so disgusting that...

804
01:34:05,645 --> 01:34:11,155
even the people with most deeds
face this fate.

805
01:34:13,495 --> 01:34:17,265
Faith starts here.

806
01:34:17,685 --> 01:34:21,655
Deeds are completed here.

807
01:34:21,845 --> 01:34:26,425
Intentions are hidden in here.

808
01:34:26,755 --> 01:34:31,335
No one can hide their intentions
from Allah.

809
01:34:31,825 --> 01:34:38,305
Because the owner of the hearts
is Allah.

810
01:34:41,525 --> 01:34:44,445
Every place we step on...

811
01:34:44,595 --> 01:34:47,345
every battle we spill our battle on...

812
01:34:47,555 --> 01:34:49,945
is to gain Allah's approval...

813
01:34:50,245 --> 01:34:54,995
and spread Allah's words.

814
01:34:56,235 --> 01:35:01,605
Allah owns everything.

815
01:35:03,995 --> 01:35:11,665
We go to battle for Allah and we
win if Allah approves it.

816
01:35:15,775 --> 01:35:18,325
İnegöl Castle

817
01:35:25,050 --> 01:35:28,600
How is the situation?
Is there anyone critical?

818
01:35:28,630 --> 01:35:31,830
We tended the wounds.
No one is heavily injured.

819
01:35:33,490 --> 01:35:36,040
Give sherbet to them.

820
01:35:36,300 --> 01:35:39,340
They need strength.

821
01:35:50,910 --> 01:35:54,460
Are they healing the men they
wounded?

822
01:35:55,490 --> 01:35:57,760
They are idiots.

823
01:36:01,620 --> 01:36:07,580
Turks say that you can't rule
with tyranny, Romanos.

824
01:36:08,040 --> 01:36:11,570
It's almost impossible to understand them.

825
01:36:16,440 --> 01:36:19,500
I see that you still love them.

826
01:36:22,420 --> 01:36:25,670
Let's not call it love.

827
01:36:26,370 --> 01:36:30,510
Getting to know them from closer.

828
01:36:30,770 --> 01:36:34,630
Getting to know your enemies
from closer.

829
01:36:48,400 --> 01:36:50,220
Lord Kosses.

830
01:36:50,450 --> 01:36:51,990
Boran.

831
01:36:53,630 --> 01:36:57,470
Osman Bey expects you and the
ambassador in the church.

832
01:37:05,180 --> 01:37:06,690
Let's go.

833
01:37:12,310 --> 01:37:15,560
Mashallah to my valiants.

834
01:37:18,390 --> 01:37:21,660
They are no different than
their ancestors.

835
01:37:22,650 --> 01:37:26,500
Thank you, my children.
Thank you.

836
01:37:26,920 --> 01:37:30,550
Holofira, thank you too.

837
01:37:31,550 --> 01:37:34,080
You saved my alps.

838
01:37:34,380 --> 01:37:37,140
It was easier to take
the castle, thanks to you.

839
01:37:37,350 --> 01:37:39,900
I'm the one grateful, Osman Bey.

840
01:37:40,270 --> 01:37:44,360
You saved my life for the second,
even third time!

841
01:37:45,860 --> 01:37:47,440
Thank you.

842
01:37:49,320 --> 01:37:53,530
Until my brother recovers,
we'll be here.

843
01:37:53,690 --> 01:37:56,920
For that reasons, prepare.

844
01:37:57,150 --> 01:38:01,480
Malhun, check my brother
all the time.

845
01:38:01,640 --> 01:38:06,410
Don't worry, my bey. Gündüz Bey
and the castle are safe with us.

846
01:38:08,190 --> 01:38:09,890
Thank you.

847
01:38:10,985 --> 01:38:16,755
Bala, as the leader of the
sisters, you deserve congratulations.

848
01:38:18,305 --> 01:38:22,465
Aygül and the sisters made
it easier for us.

849
01:38:22,655 --> 01:38:24,825
They fought with the alps.

850
01:38:26,085 --> 01:38:29,435
You revived the sisters,
thank you.

851
01:38:29,755 --> 01:38:35,225
Thank you, my bey. But I'm not involved.
The power of faith revived them.

852
01:38:35,485 --> 01:38:37,225
Thank you.

853
01:38:41,685 --> 01:38:45,845
I'm going to the ambassador now.
I'll talk to him.

854
01:38:46,355 --> 01:38:51,495
Be with my brother.
Inform me about everything.

855
01:38:51,755 --> 01:38:55,755
Don't worry, father.
My uncle is with us.

856
01:38:56,405 --> 01:38:59,145
My valiants.

857
01:38:59,405 --> 01:39:04,175
We'll help the alps now. Then, we'll
go to my uncle.

858
01:39:05,195 --> 01:39:07,495
Mashallah to my valiants.

859
01:39:08,725 --> 01:39:10,525
I should leave.

860
01:39:20,375 --> 01:39:23,625
Behold! Osman Bey!

861
01:39:36,415 --> 01:39:38,725
Speak quickly.

862
01:39:39,355 --> 01:39:45,575
At the wedding, you were invited to,
you killed the lords and took Bilecik.

863
01:39:46,045 --> 01:39:52,055
Our emperor Andrenikos demands
a great compensation from you!

864
01:40:00,345 --> 01:40:05,635
But I see that everything is out of
control. Aya Nikola is a captive.

865
01:40:06,035 --> 01:40:08,785
-İnegöl is invaded!
-Not invaded.

866
01:40:09,025 --> 01:40:12,065
Your kind does invasions.

867
01:40:13,625 --> 01:40:15,875
You'll call it a conquest.

868
01:40:17,255 --> 01:40:19,335
You'll call it a conquest, ambassador.

869
01:40:22,775 --> 01:40:24,525
Whatever.

870
01:40:24,875 --> 01:40:27,595
As the spokesman of Constantinople...

871
01:40:27,705 --> 01:40:30,295
we demand eight carts
of gold...

872
01:40:30,765 --> 01:40:32,915
return of İnegöl and Bilecik...

873
01:40:33,055 --> 01:40:39,835
and lastly, release of Aya Nikola
and his soldiers.

874
01:40:46,475 --> 01:40:48,505
Thank you.

875
01:40:50,055 --> 01:40:53,235
You spoke quickly, ambassador.

876
01:40:53,885 --> 01:40:55,965
I heard you.

877
01:40:56,665 --> 01:40:59,195
But you'll hear me too.

878
01:41:01,045 --> 01:41:04,885
We conquered Bilecik and İnegöl.

879
01:41:06,195 --> 01:41:10,615
We didn't pillage.
We didn't kill the innocent.

880
01:41:11,335 --> 01:41:16,575
For that reason, it's our
right of the sword.

881
01:41:18,755 --> 01:41:25,305
Not just you, even your emperor
can't take it from me.

882
01:41:29,865 --> 01:41:32,385
You are blowing the coals, Osman Bey!

883
01:41:32,785 --> 01:41:34,995
I'm sure that there can be
a middle ground.

884
01:41:35,225 --> 01:41:38,705
The ground is for the righteous.

885
01:41:39,735 --> 01:41:42,325
Not with traitors.

886
01:41:45,465 --> 01:41:47,235
Now, ambassador.

887
01:41:49,675 --> 01:41:51,375
I have the castles.

888
01:41:52,535 --> 01:41:55,325
And the villages around them.

889
01:41:55,885 --> 01:41:58,675
If you want your soldiers.

890
01:41:59,255 --> 01:42:03,485
I'll release them all
in return of gold.

891
01:42:07,075 --> 01:42:08,435
But.

892
01:42:11,805 --> 01:42:14,025
But except Nikola.

893
01:42:16,605 --> 01:42:21,885
There is no gold to buy Nikola,
even in Constantinople.

894
01:42:30,615 --> 01:42:31,955
Now.

895
01:42:32,425 --> 01:42:40,975
İznik, Bursa, Constantinople;
if they want to trade with us...

896
01:42:43,235 --> 01:42:48,855
they'll bring eight carts of gold to
my tribe, yearly.

897
01:42:51,635 --> 01:42:58,905
Otherwise, the eastern market is
over for the western market.

898
01:42:59,545 --> 01:43:01,085
It's so wrong.

899
01:43:01,115 --> 01:43:03,475
What you are saying is
unacceptable, Osman Bey!

900
01:43:03,475 --> 01:43:05,615
I'm not saying it for you to
accept it.

901
01:43:07,015 --> 01:43:08,735
It's my offer.

902
01:43:09,665 --> 01:43:11,175
Osman!

903
01:43:14,030 --> 01:43:20,650
Taking a few castles and killing
a few lords blinded your eyes.

904
01:43:24,740 --> 01:43:26,330
Don't forget this.

905
01:43:28,030 --> 01:43:32,350
You are still a little Turkmen bey.

906
01:43:35,500 --> 01:43:40,740
And I'll come at you with
a great army.

907
01:43:44,030 --> 01:43:48,420
Then, you'll search for a hole
to hide in.

908
01:43:51,450 --> 01:43:52,950
Romanos.

909
01:43:54,200 --> 01:43:59,290
I'll be waiting for you in the field,
not in the castle.

910
01:44:01,300 --> 01:44:03,860
Bring any army you want.

911
01:44:05,640 --> 01:44:11,230
Me and my valiants are always
ready to face you.

912
01:44:21,530 --> 01:44:25,590
Now think well.
You'll decide later.

913
01:44:34,040 --> 01:44:40,050
And, do you know why
I invited you here?

914
01:44:40,860 --> 01:44:43,420
This is the last day of
this church.

915
01:44:43,930 --> 01:44:45,930
It's our conquest customs.

916
01:44:47,130 --> 01:44:51,870
The biggest sanctuary of the castle
turns into a mosque.

917
01:44:54,910 --> 01:44:56,300
For that reason...

918
01:44:59,050 --> 01:45:00,760
make your last prayer.

919
01:45:15,630 --> 01:45:18,140
Osman. Osman.

920
01:45:20,980 --> 01:45:24,540
You should've seen it, brother.
It was a great battle.

921
01:45:26,850 --> 01:45:31,850
Kumral Abdal told us about Bedr.

922
01:45:32,910 --> 01:45:35,460
I felt like I was in it.

923
01:45:49,630 --> 01:45:51,210
What are you doing, Orhan?

924
01:45:54,960 --> 01:45:57,320
You made it bleed more.

925
01:46:01,420 --> 01:46:05,190
Why are you talking about it as if
you don't know how much I wanted it?

926
01:46:06,300 --> 01:46:07,860
I already missed it.

927
01:46:08,670 --> 01:46:10,960
Stop crushing my heart with it.

928
01:46:17,330 --> 01:46:20,630
I'm sorry. It's my fault.

929
01:46:22,850 --> 01:46:24,420
No, Holafira.

930
01:46:25,490 --> 01:46:27,520
I wasn't destined to.

931
01:46:27,900 --> 01:46:29,940
Why would it be your fault?

932
01:46:32,960 --> 01:46:40,030
But still, Alahaddin talked
about it and it hurt me.

933
01:46:40,710 --> 01:46:42,770
I wanted to be in it.

934
01:46:53,830 --> 01:46:55,400
You will, brother.

935
01:46:55,670 --> 01:46:58,250
Many battles and conquests
are awating us.

936
01:46:59,070 --> 01:47:02,220
Bursa and Constantinople are
awaiting us.

937
01:47:02,710 --> 01:47:05,250
You'll be in them.

938
01:47:07,840 --> 01:47:11,840
We will, brother. We'll fight
shoulder to shoulder.

939
01:47:29,150 --> 01:47:33,280
No. This won't be. I should inform
Kumral Abdal.

940
01:47:36,480 --> 01:47:38,020
Aygül.

941
01:47:40,210 --> 01:47:41,730
Aygül.

942
01:47:44,360 --> 01:47:46,870
There is nothing Kumral
can do.

943
01:47:55,090 --> 01:47:56,820
It's time.

944
01:48:01,210 --> 01:48:02,910
Call Osman.

945
01:48:08,280 --> 01:48:09,860
Call Osman.

946
01:48:12,350 --> 01:48:15,860
Don't, father.
Not now.

947
01:48:16,690 --> 01:48:20,930
We just reunited.
We just reunited, father.

948
01:48:30,720 --> 01:48:33,580
-Son.
-Father.

949
01:48:40,160 --> 01:48:41,750
My son.

950
01:48:41,810 --> 01:48:45,320
No. Don't cry.

951
01:48:49,630 --> 01:48:51,160
Don't cry.

952
01:48:52,490 --> 01:48:55,580
Your father's prayers are accepted.

953
01:49:01,160 --> 01:49:06,450
Your father has fallen a martyr
from a battle.

954
01:49:11,900 --> 01:49:16,390
No. Don't cry.

955
01:49:23,780 --> 01:49:27,310
-Ayşe. Ayşe.
-Gündüz!

956
01:49:30,800 --> 01:49:34,390
Ayşe. Don't cry.

957
01:49:36,890 --> 01:49:38,930
I'm leaving but...

958
01:49:42,960 --> 01:49:47,100
I'm leaving you a son,
like a wolf.

959
01:49:53,050 --> 01:49:55,130
I won't be worried.

960
01:49:59,580 --> 01:50:01,140
My Gündüz!

961
01:50:03,250 --> 01:50:06,770
What can I do without you?

962
01:50:13,300 --> 01:50:15,030
Ayşe!

963
01:50:18,560 --> 01:50:20,360
The light of my eyes.

964
01:50:25,480 --> 01:50:28,010
You were always a good wife.

965
01:50:32,120 --> 01:50:33,980
You have my blessing.

966
01:50:37,570 --> 01:50:39,630
May Allah bless you too.

967
01:50:46,820 --> 01:50:50,620
May Allah unite us
in the afterlife.

968
01:50:52,560 --> 01:50:54,070
Inshallah.

969
01:51:06,610 --> 01:51:07,950
Father!

970
01:51:11,080 --> 01:51:12,380
Father!

971
01:51:35,970 --> 01:51:37,450
My sisters.

972
01:51:42,480 --> 01:51:47,030
We fought a lot, didn't we?

973
01:51:52,250 --> 01:51:54,790
Give me your blessings.

974
01:51:55,980 --> 01:51:58,570
It's yours, brother Gündüz.

975
01:52:01,140 --> 01:52:02,850
You too.

976
01:52:09,020 --> 01:52:11,100
It's yours, Gündüz Bey.

977
01:52:33,580 --> 01:52:40,570
Turgut Bey, use some of the gold
to repair the damaged parts of the castle.

978
01:52:41,850 --> 01:52:47,410
The rest will be shared between the
people who were harmed during the battle.

979
01:52:47,620 --> 01:52:51,630
But İnegöl needs to revive.

980
01:52:51,630 --> 01:52:55,140
For that reason, trade must
start at once.

981
01:52:55,140 --> 01:52:57,640
It'll be protected
with our lives.

982
01:52:57,730 --> 01:52:59,560
The people will be happy.

983
01:52:59,560 --> 01:53:01,120
Inshallah.

984
01:53:01,570 --> 01:53:07,200
And turning this church into a mosque
is your responsibility.

985
01:53:08,890 --> 01:53:11,410
We don't forget the non-Muslims either.

986
01:53:12,290 --> 01:53:16,330
Let's build a church fitting
their beliefs.

987
01:53:16,800 --> 01:53:18,500
Don't worry.

988
01:53:19,740 --> 01:53:21,100
Thank you.

989
01:53:34,530 --> 01:53:36,110
Aygül.

990
01:53:43,930 --> 01:53:45,720
He isn't well.

991
01:54:12,970 --> 01:54:15,710
Osman should waste his time
with his little victory.

992
01:54:16,700 --> 01:54:18,710
The war is just beginning.

993
01:54:19,350 --> 01:54:23,480
I'll set such a game that
even the devil be jealous.

994
01:54:24,530 --> 01:54:26,610
I'm awaiting your orders, Barkın Bey.

995
01:54:26,760 --> 01:54:29,270
Osman thinks of beating
the lords.

996
01:54:29,270 --> 01:54:34,900
You will go to the lord of Bursa...

997
01:54:36,290 --> 01:54:38,070
and give this letter.

998
01:54:38,530 --> 01:54:40,620
-Hüsamettin.
-My bey.

999
01:54:41,030 --> 01:54:45,090
Praise Osman's victory to the
lord of Bursa.

1000
01:54:45,920 --> 01:54:55,450
Tell him that Osman claimed to be
the bey of the all Turkmens.

1001
01:54:55,700 --> 01:55:01,790
When he reads this letter, the lord
will be an enemy to Osman.

1002
01:55:04,030 --> 01:55:10,110
I'll praise him so much that he'll
want to kill Osman tomorrow.

1003
01:55:10,110 --> 01:55:13,950
Osman thinks he is powerful for
beating the little lords.

1004
01:55:14,510 --> 01:55:18,760
The lord of Bursa will do what
they couldn't.

1005
01:55:19,720 --> 01:55:22,970
Then, he'll learn about the world.

1006
01:55:24,150 --> 01:55:30,230
Söğüt, İnegöl. There will be blood.

1007
01:55:31,750 --> 01:55:34,130
Come on. Go quickly.

1008
01:56:05,185 --> 01:56:06,535
Brother.

1009
01:56:08,135 --> 01:56:11,675
Osman. Are you here?

1010
01:56:14,885 --> 01:56:16,215
I'm here, brother.

1011
01:56:20,345 --> 01:56:21,655
I'm here.

1012
01:56:27,065 --> 01:56:28,605
Are you good?

1013
01:56:30,195 --> 01:56:31,695
Brother.

1014
01:56:34,225 --> 01:56:36,055
Listen to me well.

1015
01:56:39,975 --> 01:56:41,555
What I left behind...

1016
01:56:44,615 --> 01:56:46,775
protect them.

1017
01:56:50,395 --> 01:56:52,415
It's time, Osman.

1018
01:56:55,505 --> 01:57:03,755
My mother, father, Savcı;
they are waiting for me.

1019
01:57:16,205 --> 01:57:18,225
What are you saying, brother?

1020
01:57:20,845 --> 01:57:22,685
What are you saying?

1021
01:57:24,465 --> 01:57:26,975
We'll go to many more conquests!

1022
01:57:28,985 --> 01:57:31,555
We'll fight a lot more!

1023
01:57:34,085 --> 01:57:36,645
We'll go to many more raids, brother!

1024
01:57:40,135 --> 01:57:41,465
No!

1025
01:57:52,465 --> 01:57:53,825
No!

1026
01:58:00,325 --> 01:58:01,705
You...

1027
01:58:05,865 --> 01:58:07,185
you are...

1028
01:58:13,195 --> 01:58:15,405
you are my last foundation.

1029
01:58:24,305 --> 01:58:29,835
No. Don't say that.
Don't say that.

1030
01:58:32,775 --> 01:58:37,325
Look. You have your
children.

1031
01:58:39,525 --> 01:58:41,325
Your valiants.

1032
01:58:47,775 --> 01:58:50,445
I completed my duty, brother.

1033
01:58:52,065 --> 01:58:53,625
I'm in peace.

1034
01:58:55,125 --> 01:58:57,495
Don't worry.

1035
01:59:00,615 --> 01:59:02,335
No one should.

1036
01:59:04,255 --> 01:59:06,835
It's time for Gündüz Bey.

1037
01:59:18,655 --> 01:59:20,205
Osman.

1038
01:59:24,385 --> 01:59:27,905
My beautiful mother is waiting for me.

1039
01:59:33,045 --> 01:59:37,625
Give me your blessing.
Give me...

1040
01:59:43,185 --> 01:59:44,765
Brother.

1041
02:00:02,655 --> 02:00:04,685
You have my blessing.

1042
02:00:06,215 --> 02:00:08,005
Of course, you do.

1043
02:00:15,755 --> 02:00:18,315
You too, brother.

1044
02:00:19,095 --> 02:00:21,625
It's yours, brother.

1045
02:00:23,525 --> 02:00:25,855
It's yours, my wolf brother.

1046
02:00:36,345 --> 02:00:38,345
Be at ease.

1047
02:00:39,325 --> 02:00:41,155
What you left behind...

1048
02:00:44,225 --> 02:00:46,415
will be taken care of.

1049
02:00:54,765 --> 02:00:56,305
Father?

1050
02:01:03,315 --> 02:01:04,835
My father!

1051
02:01:09,095 --> 02:01:11,665
My father, I'm coming!

1052
02:01:15,845 --> 02:01:17,595
Your Gündüz is coming.

1053
02:01:27,255 --> 02:01:31,565
There is no God but Allah...

1054
02:01:32,515 --> 02:01:33,905
and...

1055
02:01:54,995 --> 02:01:56,695
is his prophet.

1056
02:02:07,685 --> 02:02:09,275
Brother?

1057
02:02:09,415 --> 02:02:11,485
Gündüz?

1058
02:02:12,015 --> 02:02:14,065
Gündüz?

1059
02:02:14,235 --> 02:02:16,255
Father!

1060
02:02:16,485 --> 02:02:17,815
Gündüz!

1061
02:02:34,125 --> 02:02:35,695
Brother!

1062
02:02:36,445 --> 02:02:38,015
Brother!

1063
02:03:07,385 --> 02:03:09,115
Wipe your tears.

1064
02:03:10,695 --> 02:03:12,945
You are a martyr's son.

1065
02:03:13,495 --> 02:03:14,995
Stand tall.

1066
02:03:15,255 --> 02:03:16,815
Be proud.

1067
02:03:16,905 --> 02:03:19,635
Stand tall.

1068
02:03:26,795 --> 02:03:29,035
If you allow it...

1069
02:03:33,915 --> 02:03:36,435
I'll bury my brother
in İnegöl...

1070
02:03:39,145 --> 02:03:42,425
where he became a martyr.

1071
02:04:04,695 --> 02:04:06,195
Brother.

1072
02:04:12,685 --> 02:04:15,765
İnegöl Castle

1073
02:04:55,420 --> 02:04:57,970
If want to ask something.

1074
02:04:58,090 --> 02:05:03,210
Do you lose your when you get
separated?

1075
02:05:03,780 --> 02:05:05,630
Osman is a smart man.

1076
02:05:05,630 --> 02:05:09,140
He put you together
to not get lost.

1077
02:05:09,230 --> 02:05:13,180
You together wouldn't
make one man.

1078
02:05:13,410 --> 02:05:14,990
Idiots.

1079
02:05:19,390 --> 02:05:21,660
What are you talking about, coward?

1080
02:05:21,850 --> 02:05:24,700
Look, you are in our hands.

1081
02:05:25,870 --> 02:05:32,030
You can enter an unarmed captive's
dungeon only as two.

1082
02:05:33,790 --> 02:05:37,450
But I'm the coward, is that so?

1083
02:05:38,300 --> 02:05:42,170
I get it. You are begging to
get killed.

1084
02:05:42,440 --> 02:05:45,440
But you won't die
so easily, Nikola.

1085
02:05:45,610 --> 02:05:47,950
Osman Bey will kill you.

1086
02:05:48,250 --> 02:05:50,260
Don't be impatient.

1087
02:07:14,470 --> 02:07:15,820
Behold!

1088
02:07:16,700 --> 02:07:18,250
Osman Bey!

1089
02:08:35,920 --> 02:08:37,670
What's your decision?

1090
02:08:40,470 --> 02:08:43,040
It's impossible to accept your terms.

1091
02:08:46,190 --> 02:08:47,780
Alright.

1092
02:08:57,760 --> 02:09:00,150
Aya Nikola.

1093
02:09:07,530 --> 02:09:13,910
The back of the Kayı is filed
with your dagger wounds.

1094
02:09:19,100 --> 02:09:21,690
Your tyranny has reached the sky.

1095
02:09:24,290 --> 02:09:26,450
And the sky sent me to you...

1096
02:09:27,680 --> 02:09:30,400
as its fury.

1097
02:09:35,060 --> 02:09:37,890
You were always with the enemies
within...

1098
02:09:38,530 --> 02:09:41,670
you worked with the enemies outside.

1099
02:09:42,860 --> 02:09:46,690
You were with anyone who
were an enemy...

1100
02:09:48,160 --> 02:09:49,980
to the Turks.

1101
02:09:52,490 --> 02:09:58,010
But it's time for the sword
of Justice.

1102
02:10:02,780 --> 02:10:05,380
No, Osman Bey.
You can't do this!

1103
02:10:05,940 --> 02:10:09,460
-We came here for peace. You can't--
-Don't!

1104
02:10:10,650 --> 02:10:15,680
Don't! I don't beg for my life.

1105
02:10:16,210 --> 02:10:18,980
It's not your place to beg for me.

1106
02:10:24,120 --> 02:10:26,020
You won.

1107
02:10:27,140 --> 02:10:29,040
I lost.

1108
02:10:30,690 --> 02:10:32,900
And this is what a war is.

1109
02:10:34,140 --> 02:10:36,450
One wins...

1110
02:10:37,470 --> 02:10:40,170
the other loses.

1111
02:10:40,510 --> 02:10:45,070
But I'm very happy for hurting you,
Osman Bey.

1112
02:10:46,250 --> 02:10:48,520
Now, I'll die here.

1113
02:10:49,570 --> 02:10:54,230
Then, Rome will send a great
army after you.

1114
02:10:56,380 --> 02:11:01,380
Let's see, when the angry...

1115
02:11:01,710 --> 02:11:04,750
lions step on these lands...

1116
02:11:05,120 --> 02:11:08,300
what will your little wolves do?

1117
02:11:14,750 --> 02:11:18,310
I hear it.
I hear the footsteps.

1118
02:11:19,420 --> 02:11:23,000
And I'm ready.

1119
02:11:27,210 --> 02:11:28,950
They should come.

1120
02:11:31,790 --> 02:11:34,000
They should come.

1121
02:11:35,650 --> 02:11:38,190
These lands are a home to
friends...

1122
02:11:39,300 --> 02:11:42,310
and a grave to the enemies.

1123
02:11:45,530 --> 02:11:52,180
The lions on a leash have no power
against hardened wolves.

1124
02:11:55,740 --> 02:12:02,720
The breath taken by tyrants like you
is torture to the oppressed.

1125
02:12:09,360 --> 02:12:14,130
The end of the tyrants is dying
under the sword of Justice.

1126
02:12:19,690 --> 02:12:21,620
It's time.

1127
02:12:36,280 --> 02:12:38,070
Allahu Akbar.

1128
02:13:08,750 --> 02:13:10,270
Osman Bey.

1129
02:13:11,410 --> 02:13:14,760
If your show is over, I'll return to
Constantinople...

1130
02:13:14,760 --> 02:13:17,140
to inform them about the
war you declared.

1131
02:13:17,570 --> 02:13:19,620
No.

1132
02:13:21,590 --> 02:13:23,170
Wait.

1133
02:13:25,060 --> 02:13:26,590
Wait there.

1134
02:14:11,085 --> 02:14:13,135
Don't go empty-handed.

1135
02:14:15,665 --> 02:14:18,225
Let it be a gift from me to your emperor.

1136
02:14:34,595 --> 02:14:36,985
Osman!

1137
02:14:38,495 --> 02:14:44,125
Your war with the lords is over.

1138
02:14:46,125 --> 02:14:47,505
Now...

1139
02:14:49,535 --> 02:14:53,115
you are in a war with an empire
that rules the whole world.

1140
02:15:22,025 --> 02:15:24,225
Inegöl is ours now!

1141
02:15:28,735 --> 02:15:30,305
But...

1142
02:15:32,085 --> 02:15:34,635
Şuşa in the east is also ours!

1143
02:15:35,475 --> 02:15:37,525
Gencebey!

1144
02:15:43,635 --> 02:15:46,145
Get enough alps with you.

1145
02:15:46,845 --> 02:15:49,295
And build your beylig there.

1146
02:15:51,815 --> 02:15:57,365
For the order of the world,
work for the state we'll found.

1147
02:15:57,595 --> 02:15:59,345
As you order, my bey.

1148
02:15:59,685 --> 02:16:03,065
These lands belong to the Turks,
or no one at all!

1149
02:16:04,945 --> 02:16:06,525
Thank you.

1150
02:16:21,635 --> 02:16:24,165
For Allah's words...

1151
02:16:25,505 --> 02:16:28,955
we became famous by the
revenge we'll take from the shirk!

1152
02:16:29,475 --> 02:16:31,165
Tend your wounds!

1153
02:16:32,945 --> 02:16:35,045
Sharpen your swords!

1154
02:16:36,945 --> 02:16:39,763
Now is not the time to stop
the conquests!

1155
02:16:40,395 --> 02:16:43,945
Now is time for jihad!

1156
02:16:44,084 --> 02:16:45,674
Allahu Akbar!

1157
02:16:45,754 --> 02:16:54,315
Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar!

1158
02:16:54,325 --> 02:17:06,155
Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar!

1159
02:17:06,183 --> 02:17:14,214
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com